e corpus.\n\nI'm fairly confident B-6 is correct based on code reading. But the prompt says to verify with live probes \"where possible\". The probes require approval. Let me try once more with a simpler, clearly-safe command to see if the approval is granted, or try the test runner.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The permission issue: my `clojure -M -e` probe was gated with \"This command requires approval\". The `git`, `grep`, `find` (in allowed dirs), `cat`, `sha256sum` commands worked. The clojure execution is a heavier action.\n\nGiven the constraint, let me try running a targeted single test via the test runner, which might be more acceptable, OR just rely on code reading + the evidence logs (which I can read freely).\n\nActually, the evidence logs (green-jvm-regressions.log etc.) ARE the live execution evidence. I can read them. And I can also verify the red logs show the counterexamples. Let me read the new evidence logs to confirm they're clean and match claims.\n\nLet me check the evidence dir 1795710808000-floatkind-evidence.","signature":"fa9ee267-28f4-4a77-bed6-6eb16f272513"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":454,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":200192,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f2c1e4a-7b3d-4e8f-a6c5-d0e9f8a1b2c3","uuid":"55f33494-1b46-46a4-a23b-66044a610b74","timestamp":"2026-11-26T17:22:39.990Z","thinking_duration_ms":64429,"thinking_display":"updates"}
